 "notes": "Placeholder site, about 450 m east of the Hurghada harbour breakwater: the name 'Hurghada Wave' is most likely a boat, and the site is set on the El Mina (El Minya) wreck off Hurghada harbour. The map shows the 58 x 8.5 m T-43 minesweeper lying on her port side, bow at about 26 m, stern at 32 m, the bomb hole at 19 m and the mooring on the stern. Position, size and depths from the Red Sea Wreck Project (27°13.543'N 33°50.861'E); the NW-SE orientation from aquariusredsea.com, with the bow assumed to point north-west; the Hassabella trawler a few minutes' swim away is left off because its bearing is unknown. Positions are approximate.",
